<title>NETHERLANDS: Unilever guilder shares jump.</title>
<headline>Unilever guilder shares jump.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-11-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Unilever NV/Plc jumped 13.40 guilders or 5.20 percent to 272.00 in early Friday Amsterdam trade, enlivened by the firm's report of third quarter figures, which were at the upper end of analysts' forecasts.</p>
<p>Unilever reported a 1.31 billion guilder net profit at current exchange rates, up from the previous 1.22 billion and at the upper end of the 1.15 to 1.33 billion forecast range.</p>
<p>Analysts said the third quarter net exceptional charge of 81 million guilders was lower than anticipated and this was also helping the shares, although profit-taking might kick in later in the session on speculation of a big fourth quarter charge. -- Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
